id: pm-rl-policycards
title: Explain learned policy suitability with portable replayable cards
description: "Export minimized policy suitability, scope, action limits, regressions and evidence digests across agent backends; automatically retain explanations throughout recursive candidate and promotion paths."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#100"
created_at: "2026-10-23T14:29:56.651Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T21:05:33.229Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Missing provenance blocks adoption; replay identifies every cited result; export contains no training examples or credentials; typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON CLI; every recursive candidate and promotion has a card; read-only public tracker validation demonstrates at least two generations; npm and Bun CI release gates pass at unchanged thresholds.
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[38]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T14:31:01.471Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: current host CLI is 2026.10.23; package SDK remains pinned at 2026.10.20. Inspected CLI command ownership and pm-context context-pack explanations: neither exports learned-policy suitability. Existing pm-rl checkpoint artifacts retain executable state; generation provenance, causal plans, shadow comparisons and recursive improver receipts own the evidence. Cards will reuse SDK complete inventory, certified history reads and content-addressed package hashes. No dependency bump, trainer replacement or context assembler. Plan: minimized digest-only cards, replay/adoption refusals, automatic recursive candidate/outcome publication, non-Git public-copy validation for two generations, targeted local checks and full npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-23T14:43:18.298Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed export/replay/adoption-check SDK and CLI, bounded digest-only projection, exact timestamped history citations and retained candidate/promotion cards. Recursive durable phases now retain outcome cards plus one card per proposed configuration/recipe. Local typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring checks passed before the last small additions; targeted regression work is ongoing. Verified the selected pm-ops commit is publicly accessible and MIT licensed; prepared a read-only non-Git copy for two-generation numerical-policy acceptance. Full release gates will run in CI because the shared host is saturated."
  "2026-10-23T14:54:41.570Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabled only recordRecursivePolicyCards publication; the durable recursive-phase regression failed with 0 retained cards versus 6 required. Restored implementation; targeted suite passed 8/8 with no skips, new module 100% lines/functions and 98.35% branches before final branch cases. The first real-data run passed two promotions, 5 retained cards, 19 replayed citations, 105 training plus 41 held-out items and unchanged 300-file source digest. Compact output measured 2082-2085 JSON bytes and 1544-1547 TOON bytes. Final packed rerun and CI gates pending."
  "2026-10-23T15:03:12.890Z",codex-agent,"PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/100 (ready for review). Final public-copy run: 146 items, 105 training/41 held-out, 512 collected samples, two promoted generations, five retained cards, 19 replayed cited results and one replay of the earlier policy during generation two. All 300 source files retain the same digest; packed CLI JSON 2082-2085 bytes and TOON 1544-1547 bytes. Source addresses are SDK-normalized for portability. Targeted shadow promotion passed without Git after completing fixture provenance. Linked snapshot regression suite passed 8/8; typed limits and serialization boundary regression also passed. CI release gates remain pending and will be reported on the PR; superseded queued run canceled before execution. No CLI/SDK defect was identified; numerical snapshot recognition does not establish proposer transfer."
  "2026-10-23T15:25:49.315Z",codex-agent,"CI caught a feature integration error, not a pm SDK defect: adding explanatory fields inside replay-critical trainer configurations caused resume/status comparisons to fail. Moving that metadata to native SDK notes preserves the original training receipts and their exact replay contract. Creation-history coordinates also keep seed cards stable across claims/comments so failed resumes do not add card artifacts. Completing peer-edit fixture provenance while retaining its concurrency/rollback assertions. The new card module itself measured 100% lines/branches/functions in the failed full-gate run; complete gates will be rerun after regression fixes."
  "2026-10-23T15:37:13.357Z",codex-agent,"Correction validated on the read-only public copy: both generations now also resume and report status successfully, with two resumed generations and the same final checkpoint. Five cards and 19 cited results remain, with unchanged source bytes and the same measured JSON/TOON sizes. Targeted SDK fault/concurrency and bandit/LM resume checks pass; one parallel local train-fault case hit the unchanged 120-second host limit and is being retried alone. Native evaluation notes preserve the exact original trainer configuration. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings and changelog checks remain required; full npm/Bun CI will be rerun at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T15:38:17.535Z",codex-agent,"Corrected targeted card suite passed 8/8 with zero fail/skip/cancel and 100% module lines, branches and functions. Public-copy validation passed two promotions, generation-two replay of the earlier card, two resumed generations and matching status/final checkpoint; source digest unchanged. Bandit/LM rerun and concurrency/rollback targets passed. Lint, duplication, docstring and test typecheck passed. A parallel local train-fault timeout is being checked in isolation without changing its bound. Full-gate CI on the corrected commit is the remaining acceptance evidence and will be linked with exact counts in the PR."
  "2026-10-23T15:39:32.622Z",codex-agent,"The isolated train-fault regression passed 1/1 in 19.1 seconds under its original 120-second bound, resolving the combined-run host timeout without a threshold change. All targeted regressions now have passing evidence. Proceeding with the full npm/Bun CI matrix on the corrected source."
  "2026-10-23T15:50:39.965Z",codex-agent,"Auditing one final publication boundary: after promotion commits, an IO failure can prevent its outcome card from being written. Resume must publish that missing card from verified committed evidence before advancing. Adding a real filesystem obstruction test around the real SDK close, with no fabricated SDK results, and recovery in the verified complete/refused generation branches."
  "2026-10-23T16:12:59.356Z",codex-agent,"Full CI run 39980189474 passed every npm/Bun job at unchanged thresholds on commit 5502f77. Node 26 npm and Bun each measured 752/752 tests, zero fail/skip, and 100/100/100/100 across 51 source files. Added final recovery proof: a real post-close filesystem obstruction first left zero promoted cards after resume (expected one); recovery now passes. Both native storage failure and real SDK card-identity collision cases pass (3/3 including their parent), as do refused/budget-exhausted replay targets (2/2). Publisher failures are separated from promotion-decision refusals; verified resume repairs missing outcome cards before advancing, with final refusals recorded through native notes ifAbsent. Final commit and its full CI rerun remain pending."
  "2026-10-23T16:17:44.347Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: Node 22 also passed 752/752 in the green baseline CI run, with all four coverage dimensions at 100% over 51 files. Post-commit publication recovery passes 3/3 and refusal replay passes 2/2; final public-copy rerun still retains five cards and replays 19 citations across two promoted/resumed generations. Receipt now also states the descriptive majority baseline (36/41 = 0.8780487804878049); sampled policy means 0.59765/0.685825 remain below it. This is card provenance/lifecycle evidence, not a model-quality certification. Final source gates will be reported on the PR after completion."
  "2026-10-23T16:29:41.336Z",codex-agent,"Strengthened the evidence domain to include collection-policy, environment, checkpoint and parent metadata, in addition to body/type/version/status and evaluation notes. This makes adoption detect changes to material provenance fields while historical replay continues to identify the original cited results. The targeted regression changes a real collection Run policy field and requires the old card to refuse adoption."
  "2026-10-23T16:31:03.535Z",codex-agent,"The material-provenance regression passed: historical replay remains valid after a real collection-policy metadata edit, while adoption of the stale card refuses. The public-copy run also passed with the expanded digest domain, two resumed/promoted generations, five retained cards and 19 resolved citations. No trainer receipts or gate thresholds changed. Superseded CI run 39985764379 was canceled for the final digest hardening; the previously completed run 39980189474 remains green baseline evidence. Waiting for full release gates on the final committed source."
  "2026-10-23T16:57:18.949Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI exposed one valid legacy-reference compatibility case: a Generation approval stored in uppercase resolves through the SDK but the card identifier guard rejected it before lookup. Allowing ASCII case in input validation delegates resolution to the SDK; exported evidence still uses the canonical SDK item id. Reusing the existing mixed-approval-alias resume regression and adding an uppercase export equivalence assertion. Bun completed 755 tests with this single failure; targeted verification and final gates are being rerun."
  "2026-10-23T17:08:57.821Z",codex-agent,"Alias compatibility verification: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"mixed approval aliases\" test/meta.test.ts passed 1/1, zero fail/skip. The minimized-card canonical/uppercase export regression passed 1/1. Reverting only the case-insensitive identifier guard made that regression fail with card_invalid; restored the guard. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring and git diff --check passed. The previous full CI matrix completed 755 tests per job with 754 passing and this single alias failure. Final release gates will rerun on the corrected source at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T18:02:17.576Z",codex-agent,"Review blocked three acceptance properties: adoption must certify retained cards and evidence through the full root ancestry; policy identity must bind the checkpoint artifact plus configuration instead of evaluation-only metadata; operational read faults must remain retryable rather than terminal promotion refusals. Branch pulled and main checked: no new main commits to merge. Reusing this item. Each fix will receive a real-tracker regression and isolated behavioral revert proof, then targeted checks and exact-head npm/Bun CI."
  "2026-10-23T18:15:55.768Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes implemented: adoption certifies retained current cards and all cited evidence through the canonical root ancestry; missing roots, cards, root-only evidence and cycles fail closed. Policy identity now binds content-addressed checkpoint/policy references plus configuration; evaluation notes do not redefine a policy. Unfitted proposals expose proposal_digest with a null policy_digest and cannot be adopted. Native operational read faults use provenance_read_retryable, and only explicit policy/permission verdict codes are terminal promotion refusals. Initial three review regressions passed; dedicated suite passed 14/14 before expanded ancestry edge cases. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring gates passed. Isolated revert proofs and updated public-copy evidence are underway."
  "2026-10-23T18:25:56.650Z",codex-agent,"Isolated behavioral revert proofs completed, one fix at a time with all other fixes retained. Removing only the adoption ancestry verification made \"adoption requires every ancestor generation, retained card and cited result through the root\" fail: missing expected rejection after deleting the grandparent. Restoring configuration-only policy hashing made \"policy identity binds checkpoint content and configuration independently of evaluation notes\" fail on equal digests for distinct checkpoints. Restoring only the old snapshot catch made \"operational card reads are typed retryable errors and promotion remains resumable\" fail with missing expected rejection: the one-shot EIO was converted into a terminal promotion refusal. Each reverted run exited 1; all fixes were restored exactly. The complete dedicated suite passed 14/14 with no skips before the final stricter SDK read classifier and opaque-reference case; the restored three regressions are being rerun. Public-copy validation passed two promoted/resumed generations, five retained cards and 19 citations, with all 300 source files unchanged; final JSON measures 2173-2176 bytes and TOON 1630-1633 bytes."
  "2026-10-23T18:30:57.178Z",codex-agent,"Restored verification completed: the PM-linked snapshot command for the three review regressions passed 3/3, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Expanded ancestry coverage includes missing grandparent, missing root card, root-only missing evidence, corrupted card body/version/type, opaque policy identity, unpromoted ancestry and cycles. Targeted durable read-fault, unreadable collection provenance and exhausted approval checks passed 3/3. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run duplicates, npm run docstring and git diff --check passed. The public-copy receipt and example were refreshed for the artifact/configuration identity and separate proposal digest. CI npm/Bun release gates will run on the committed source at unchanged thresholds; final counts and run links will be retained in PR 100."
  "2026-10-23T19:03:49.443Z",codex-agent,"Review recovery at 9984f1c: branch clean and origin/main fully included (7 commits ahead, zero behind). GraphQL returned zero review threads. Latest CodeRabbit issue comment 6367880008 explicitly skips automatic review; no submitted CodeRabbit review or outside-diff findings exist. CI run 40004001649 fails six existing read-error/author propagation tests after retryable provenance handling. Preserve original nontransient storage and coordinator errors while keeping transient reads typed and resumable."
  "2026-10-23T19:06:28.789Z",codex-agent,"All six failing CI scenarios now pass directly, together with the existing transient-card resumability test (7/7). Added regression coverage for preserving unrelated native read/coordinator errors, and fixed a second transient-read-to-permanent-drift conversion in evaluation-plan creation history. Typecheck and lint pass; behavioural revert proofs are running independently without modifying tests."
  "2026-10-23T19:07:41.206Z",codex-agent,"Five independent behavioural reverts each failed exactly 1/1 selected regression (exit 1, assertion failures; tests unchanged; production source restored immediately): (1) adoptPolicyCard without verifyCardAncestry: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"adoption requires every ancestor\" test/policy-card.test.ts; (2) assemble policy_digest reverted to configuration/proposal hash: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"policy identity binds\" test/policy-card.test.ts; (3) snapshot blanket missing-provenance catch: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"operational card reads\" test/policy-card.test.ts; (4) rethrowOperationalRead substituting unrelated native errors: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"unrelated native\" test/policy-card.test.ts; (5) createdItem blanket eval_plan_drift catch: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"transient creation-history\" test/evaluation-plan.test.ts. Restored original durable-loop read-failure assertion so unrelated errors retain diagnostic identity. Tests import source; dist is untracked."
  "2026-10-23T19:14:27.902Z",codex-agent,"Self-review completed across policy-card assembly/replay/adoption, ancestry, durable publication/resume and promotion catches. No further policy-identity or ancestry bypass found. Pinned merge install refreshed generated .gitattributes; isolated-HOME strict tracker health passes. Normal-home health sees an unrelated globally installed extension host-version skew; isolated CI identity removes it. Existing stale-item/provenance advisories remain advisory; no history repair performed. Full Node 26 npm release gate is running at unchanged thresholds under shared host load; linked no-PM-context snapshot tests are also running."
  "2026-10-23T19:19:11.475Z",codex-agent,"The broad linked snapshot suite hit its 600-second runner timeout under shared host load: 29 evaluation-plan tests and the first policy-card test had passed, with zero assertion failures before interruption. Retrying the five directly relevant regressions as a focused linked command; full release gates still include both complete files. Two unrelated subprocess timing cases in the npm full run passed unchanged on immediate isolated retry (2/2): stream transport reports real spawn/exit/signal/consumer/timeout failures, and real broken stdin pipe."
  "2026-10-23T19:26:05.894Z",codex-agent,"Source and regression fixes pushed as 0ba3edf; full npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26 release gates are running in CI run 40010769742, all past strict tracker health. The duplicate local npm run passed typecheck/build/lint/duplicates/docstrings/publish attestation and the large-learner regression, but its two subprocess timing failures already passed unchanged on focused retry (2/2). Stopped that duplicate full run to reduce host contention; no local full-gate pass is claimed. Final complete gate evidence will come from CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T19:27:34.198Z",codex-agent,"Restored production verified by pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"adoption requires every ancestor|policy identity binds|operational card reads|unrelated native|transient creation-history\" test/policy-card.test.ts test/evaluation-plan.test.ts passed 5/5, zero failures/skips/cancellations (snapshot workspace, PM context none, Node 26). Together with all five assertion-failing behavioural reverts and the six formerly failing CI scenarios plus resumability passing 7/7, this establishes the regression proofs. CodeQL run 40010769603 passed; complete release CI run 40010769742 is pending."
  "2026-10-23T19:32:45.612Z",codex-agent,"Final error-shape audit found native DOM TimeoutError carries numeric code 23, so code-string matching alone preserved it as an untyped error. Extended the real-SDK operational-read regression with this native timeout and classified TimeoutError by its native error name, while retaining unrelated native/coordinator diagnostics. Running focused acceptance and a separate behavioural revert before pushing this additional timeout fix."
  "2026-10-23T19:33:09.673Z",codex-agent,"Native timeout fix proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"operational card reads\" test/policy-card.test.ts passes 1/1 with native TimeoutError included, and typecheck/lint pass. Removing only the TimeoutError-name branch from rethrowOperationalRead makes exactly that regression fail 1/1, exit 1, with native TimeoutError instead of provenance_read_retryable. Restored the branch immediately; tests unchanged. This is a sixth independent behavioural revert proof."
  "2026-10-23T19:57:58.040Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40012369395 at 6fba6b0: npm Node 22 and Bun Node 26 release gates both passed 760/760 tests, zero failures/skips, with all 51 source files measured at 100% lines/branches/functions/statements. Native TimeoutError regression is included. npm Node 26 is still running. The final focused linked snapshot run also passed 5/5 at Node 26 after the native-timeout change, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All six independent revert proofs are recorded above."
  "2026-10-23T20:00:10.085Z",codex-agent,"Complete release verification at 6fba6b0 in CI run 40012369395: npm run release:check on Node 22 passed 760/760; npm run release:check on Node 26 passed 760/760; bun run release:check on Node 26 passed 760/760. Each measured all 51 source files at 100% statements/lines/branches/functions, zero test failures/skips. Strict tracker health, identity/privacy, production audit, package dry run and changelog checks passed; CodeQL passed. Earlier local subprocess timing failures passed unchanged on focused retry (2/2) and all full CI gates. Broad linked runner timeout was replaced by focused 5/5 passes; both complete files pass in full CI. Stopped remaining duplicate local gate after complete CI acceptance; no local full-gate pass is claimed. Six independent assertion-failing behavioural reverts are recorded above. No review threads were replied to or resolved; CodeRabbit skipped review and Greptile reported an expired trial. The item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-23T20:00:12.513Z",codex-agent,"Bookkeeping: one file-link event used the detected harness:codex identity before the explicit author export; later writes explicitly use codex-agent. Existing history was preserved append-only. No history repair or re-anchoring was performed."
  "2026-10-23T20:21:38.649Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI exposed a separate staging TOCTOU race: Node 22 passed 759/760 but the checkpoint-only Compose case failed when completion.json disappeared between readdir and lstat in stagingBytes. This is an actual filesystem race, not a timeout; fixing it within release-gate recovery. Missing listed entries now contribute zero current retained bytes, while missing staging directories, links/directories and missing completion receipts still refuse. Added a real-filesystem deletion at the enumeration boundary with no SDK mock."
  "2026-10-23T20:23:12.584Z",codex-agent,"Staging race regression passes 2/2 with existing completion-integrity coverage on both Node 22 and Node 26: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"staging measurement|completion validation refuses\" test/process.test.ts. Reverting only stagingBytes to its previous lstat behavior makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"staging measurement\" test/process.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1, with ERR_ASSERTION from the real ENOENT. Restored the exact source immediately. The test removes an actual completion file after native directory enumeration, checks retained-byte accounting, and still requires the typed missing-receipt refusal. No SDK mock or timing-based race is used. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-10-23T20:25:11.185Z",codex-agent,"Read every failed check in CI run 40015852948 with gh run view --log-failed: one Node 22 staging-entry deletion race (759/760) was the sole failure; npm Node 26 and Bun passed 760/760 with full 100% coverage. The race is now fixed in stagingBytes with a native nonthrowing missing-entry stat; other filesystem errors and unsafe entries still fail. Linked staging tests pass 2/2, as do direct Node 22/26 runs, and the seventh independent behavioural revert fails deterministically. Build, typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring checks pass. Seven revert proofs and 5/5 policy/history plus 2/2 staging linked results are retained. Final release CI will validate the next pushed head at unchanged thresholds; no new permission or review authority is implied."
  "2026-10-23T21:00:46.657Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched remote head 0a46d8e; main is fully included. Complete GraphQL reviewThreads read returned zero threads; no CodeRabbit review body or outside-diff findings exists (automatic review skipped). Verified both supplied blockers: minimizing scores are treated as regressions, and prospective approval citations can overflow a card after promotion commits. Plan: direction-aware regression classification and in-lock prospective-card validation before promotion writes; regressions and independent behavioural revert proofs, full unchanged npm/Bun release gates. SDK pin remains unchanged; current registry CLI is 2026.10.23."
  "2026-10-23T21:04:12.509Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared prospective export validation inside the promotion writer lock, before update/close; the promoted body contributes approval citations, numeric limits, direction-aware regressions and outcome bytes. Both manual and recursive promotion callers use this core. Self-review found one generation regression comparison and no second irreversible promotion writer. Direction regression passes for minimizing/maximizing improvements, ties and regressions. A separate long-identifier SDK lock refusal discovered during fixture construction is tracked by pm-rl-longidlock; no upstream report filed."
  "2026-10-23T21:05:16.441Z",codex-agent,"Two independent behavioural reverts proved the fixes: (1) restoring only the maximization comparison in source makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"policy regressions respect\" test/policy-card.test.ts fail 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION (reward_regression incorrectly emitted for minimizing improvement); (2) removing only the in-lock validatePromotedPolicyCard call makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"prospective promoted card overflow\" test/policy-card.test.ts fail 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION because candidate body changed to promoted despite card_limit. Each exited 1; production source restored in finally; test SHA-256 unchanged. Restored direction scenarios passed 1/1 and overflow passed 1/1: two failed attempts preserve body/status/updated_at/card digest, then a smaller candidate consumes the same one-unit approval and retains a replayable promoted card. Tests import source; dist is untracked."
  "2026-10-23T21:05:33.229Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test pm-rl-policycards --run --only-last --progress passed both new regressions, 2/2, zero failures/skips/cancellations, in its snapshot workspace with PM context none. Full release gate is running with isolated HOME and global/system Git configuration disabled, Node 26, at the unchanged four 100-percent thresholds. npm ci completed with zero audit vulnerabilities. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication (zero clones across 51 files), docstrings (378 declarations), and changelog generation/check passed. No CodeRabbit finding was available to reject; no GitHub review thread exists to reply to or resolve."
